          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note0",
          "literal": "Котелок — жёсткая фетровая шляпа с куполообразной тульей и узкими полями.",
          "literalSHA256": "c9e7af424f2ccc2f243a7c214b81abc6bb198c0f9b806da414c097aa264e18ae",
          "primaryGround": "The linked derby sense defines a bowler/derby as a stiff felt hat with dome-shaped crown and narrow brim.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17bfa/source-fashion28-cycle1/mw-derby.json"
          ],
          "locator": [
            "mw-derby.json, captured full page, sense 4 L59-L62; kids sense L138-L140"
          ],
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17bfa/source-fashion28-cycle1/mw-derby.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note1",
          "literal": "Первое известное употребление слова fedora в этом значении датируется 1883 годом.",
          "literalSHA256": "c2e1141aaa846ec944cfce1c9e0587774c0bd8c98467213b7266a488922511b8",
          "primaryGround": "The retained fedora entry gives 1883 as the first known use in this meaning, an additional fact about the correct hat.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17b9e/source-fashion26/raw/mw-fedora.json"
          ],
          "locator": [
            "mw-fedora.json, captured full page, simple definition L38-L40; first-known-use L54-L60"
